# Cursor Rules

## Primary Language
- Use Python as the primary programming language
- Follow PEP 8 style guidelines
- Use type hints where appropriate

## Code Style
- Write functional, clean code
- Avoid excessive comments and docstrings
- Focus on self-documenting code
- Keep functions small and focused
- Use meaningful variable and function names

## AWS Deployment
- Prefer AWS services for deployment
- Use Terraform or AWS CDK for infrastructure as code
- Follow AWS best practices and security guidelines
- Use AWS managed services when possible

## Git Practices
- Make frequent git commits with short, relevant messages
- Use conventional commit format when appropriate
- Keep commits atomic and focused on single changes
- Write clear, descriptive commit messages

## General Guidelines
- Write testable code
- Use dependency injection where appropriate
- Follow SOLID principles
- Keep dependencies minimal and up-to-date
- Use environment variables for configuration 